[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_0
diagnosis_text:
The affected component is the BGP control plane on leaf_router_0_0 (FRRouting/bgpd daemon). From pc_0_0, ping to 10.0.1.2 returns “Destination Net Unreachable” from 10.0.0.1, which is pc_0_0’s default gateway on leaf_router_0_0. On that leaf, the routing table contains only directly connected routes (10.0.0.0/24 and its two spine uplinks), with no route to 10.0.1.0/24. “show ip bgp summary” on leaf_router_0_0 reports “bgpd is not running,” and systemctl shows frr.service is failed. This explains the symptom: with bgpd down, leaf_router_0_0 does not learn or advertise any fabric routes, so it generates ICMP net-unreachable for 10.0.1.0/24.

Fabric health elsewhere looks good. Both spines have established BGP to the other leaf (leaf_router_0_1) and have learned 10.0.1.0/24 (e.g., spine_router_0_0 shows B>* 10.0.1.0/24 via 172.16.0.7). Each spine’s BGP neighbor to leaf_router_0_0 is stuck Active (172.16.0.5 and 172.16.0.9), consistent with bgpd being down on that leaf. Super-spine BGP is also established.

Root cause: FRR/bgpd is not running on leaf_router_0_0, leaving it with only connected routes and breaking reachability for 10.0.1.0/24.

Corrective fix: Restart FRR on leaf_router_0_0 (restart the frr service), verify bgpd comes up and BGP sessions to both spines establish, and confirm 10.0.1.0/24 appears in the routing table. No restart is needed on spine_router_0_0.
=== END ===